Currently the lint version on our Tru64 server (OSF1  V5.1 732)
supports 2 flags that control what lint uses for proprocessing source
code  cc, and cpp.

I would like to use neither, I would like to use gcc to preprocess our
code.  The cpp and cc methods of precompiling are not as featured as
gcc.

Is there an updated lint, or updated cpp/cc for this version of tru64
that we can use?   The specific bit of code that lint chews on is:

#define func(type, fmt, args...)    \
           func( type, __FUNCTION__, __LINE__, fmt, ## args)

Under GNU this is valid syntax, but alas under cc/cpp it is not
recognized and generates a tonne of warnings.


