Not as far as I know today (and I've been known to be wrong).  A future 
version is suppose to support the "mount -o extend" option which I think 
should work for the root file system.  This would require that the 
logically contiguous blocks following the current root volume be 
incorporated into the root volume.  So if you stopped using the 'b' 
partition, them modified the disklabel to include the space from 'b' 
into the 'a' partition, then used the mount -o extent option, you may be 
able to extend the root volume "IN A FUTURE RELEASE".   If the root is 
on an LSM volume or a RAID/SAN type controller that allows extending an 
existing volume it might be easier, but again this will only be an 
option in a "FUTURE RELEASE".

Since this is not available today, anything could happen to the proposed 
functionality between now and when the next release ships.  Your mileage 
may vary, object appear smaller in the review view mirror, etc...

                                        Bob Harris


