If by "re-installing", you mean wipe the disk clean and start over from the 
CDROM, then yes, you can expand the /root filesystem.  However, it's not 
really expanding the root filesystem.  It's really vdump everything off to 
tape or another disk, boot the CDROM, get to a shell prompt, repartition 
the disk and vrestore everything back again.  Not trivial, not for the 
faint of heart, but not impossible.  If you have a spare disk, it's a lot 
easier and less nerve-wracking.

        Stu


