Perl has builtin support for treating DBM files as hash tables.  The following
Perl script should suffice to provide the information in the DBM version of
/etc/passwd:

	#!/usr/bin/perl -w

	use strict;

	dbmopen(%PASSWD, "/etc/passwd", undef)
		or die "Cannot open password database";

	while (my ($key, $value) = each (%DATA)) {
		print "$key:$value\n";
	}

Hope that helps.

