I don't know what the web "driver development" tool produces, I've
never used it, but PCI drivers do support user access to PCI card space,
I am currently working with a driver that does just that.

I will warn you to be VERY careful about mmap'ing PCI register space
into user space for general manipulations. The security implications,
danger level, and potential for misuse are very high. The first thing
I am doing with the driver I inherited is remove this facility to make
all accesses through regulated IOCTL commands.

