alex <alexandre.masselot@bigfoot.com> writes:

> I cannot figure out why gcc cannot link the following file:
> >cat a.cpp
...
> /usr/bin/ld:
> Unresolved:
> gethostbyname(char const *)

What this means is that 'gethostbyname' has aquired C++ linkage,
and the linker is now looking for gethostbyname__FPCc (which
is not there).

So it is a compilation problem. However I can not reproduce this
using gcc-2.95.3 on a 5.0 system.

Perhaps if you add 'extern "C" struct hostent *gethostbyname(const char *);'
somewhere after 'netdb.h' gcc will either stop C++mangling or tell you
where "bad" gethostbyname prototype is coming from.

Cheers,
-- 
